 Also called: Tiled Fractal Noise
 ## Overview
-Fractal Value Noise with Domain Warping is a multi-scale procedural noise technique that generates seamless tiled volume data by warping the input coordinate space before sampling [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of directional stripe artifacts common in standard tiled noise by using independent lattices for warping and sampling, ensuring isotropic, organic patterns without fixed-direction periodicity [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Tiled Value Noise](8293-tiled-value-noise.md) by adding non-linear coordinate distortion and fractal summation.
